<title>UK: Hambros up on SBC Warburg comments.</title>
<headline>Hambros up on SBC Warburg comments.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK financial services group Hambros jumped to a three-month high after brokerage SBC Warburg raised its profit forecasts on one of Hambros' partly owned subsidiaries, dealers said.</p>
<p>While the brokerage maintained its &quot;hold &quot;rating on Hambros shares, Warburg recommended the stock as a &quot;trading buy&quot; based on the asset valuation of its 52 percent owned subsidiary Countrywide, they said.</p>
<p>By 1231 GMT, the shares were up 23p, or 9.7 percent, to 260p.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
